---
import Base from '../layouts/Base.astro';
// Text copied from the "Privacy, Use and Disposal Statement" Google Doc. Edit there first, then here.
---
<Base title="Privacy, Use, and Disposal Statement" current="/privacy" description="How Mind Shift Collective handles the information you share with us.">
  <section style="padding-top:88px;padding-bottom:88px;">
    <div class="wrap" style="max-width:760px;">
      <p class="eyebrow">Privacy</p>
      <h1 style="font-size:clamp(36px,5vw,52px);">Privacy, Use, and Disposal Statement</h1>
      <div class="stack" style="gap:18px;color:var(--ink-2);margin-top:24px;">
        <p>At Mind Shift Health, Inc., we are committed to protecting the trust you place in us. We recognize that the information you share, whether personal experiences, mental health details, or other sensitive materials, is deeply personal, and we handle it with care, respect, and confidentiality.</p>
        <h2>Privacy</h2>
        <p>All information you provide is treated as confidential. We collect and use information only as necessary to support our community and the programs we provide. Personal details will not be shared with third parties without your explicit consent, except where required by law. You have the right to access, correct, or request the removal of your information, and we will make every reasonable effort to honor your requests promptly.</p>
        <h2>Community Directory</h2>
        <p>Our community directory is designed to help members connect, share resources, and support one another. Participation is entirely voluntary. You control what information is included and who can access it. Directory information will never be shared publicly without your consent, and you may update or remove your details at any time.</p>
        <h2>Company Listings</h2>
        <p>We list an organization on our site only after a person authorized to act for it gives written consent through our <a href="/companies/consent">Company Listing Consent</a> form. Consent can be withdrawn at any time by emailing us, and the listing will be removed promptly.</p>
        <h2>Use of Contributions</h2>
        <p>The insights, stories, and materials you share may be used to improve programs, share educational content, or strengthen the community. Any such use will be conducted thoughtfully and in accordance with your stated permissions.</p>
        <h2>Slack Group, known as Mind Shift Collective</h2>
        <p>The Mind Shift Collective Slack group is intended solely for community members to discuss, interact, and support each other in a respectful and confidential environment. Participation is voluntary, and conversations within the group should align with our privacy and community guidelines.</p>
        <h2>Information We Collect</h2>
        <p>We collect personal information that you provide directly to us as well as information collected automatically through cookies or similar technologies as needed to support our services.</p>
        <h2>How We Use Your Information</h2>
        <p>Your personal data is used to:</p>
        <ul><li>Provide, operate, and maintain our community and programs</li><li>Personalize your experience and improve our services</li><li>Communicate relevant updates and program information</li><li>Comply with legal obligations</li></ul>
        <h2>Data Sharing and Disclosure</h2>
        <p>We do not sell your information. Data may only be shared with trusted service providers who support our operations under strict confidentiality or as required by law.</p>
        <h2>CCPA Rights (for California residents)</h2>
        <p>If you reside in California, you have the right to:</p>
        <ul><li>Access and know what personal information we collect, use, share, or sell</li><li>Request deletion of your personal information, subject to legal exceptions</li><li>Opt-out of the sale or sharing of your personal information</li><li>Not be discriminated against for exercising your privacy rights</li></ul>
        <p>We provide at least two methods for submitting privacy requests, including phone, email, or web form.</p>
        <h2>Data Retention and Disposal</h2>
        <p>We retain your information only as long as necessary to fulfill the purposes described or as required by law. When no longer needed, information is disposed of securely through:</p>
        <ul><li>Permanent deletion of digital records</li><li>Destruction of physical materials</li></ul>
        <h2>Security</h2>
        <p>We implement reasonable administrative, technical, and physical safeguards to protect your information from unauthorized access or disclosure.</p>
        <h2>Contact Us</h2>
        <p>For questions, privacy requests, or more information, please contact us at <a href="mailto:hello@mindshiftcollective.net">hello@mindshiftcollective.net</a>.</p>
        <h2>Updates to This Policy</h2>
        <p>Mind Shift Health, Inc. may update this statement as needed to reflect changes in practices or legal requirements. Updated versions will be posted with an effective date.</p>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>
</Base>
